From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 02:45:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 49/49] MIPS: configs: ad5x: Optimise the kernel for
 performance

The defconfig had the kernel built for size (-Os). On this printer the
kernel's hot paths (networking, fork, context switches) run measurably
faster at -O2, for a compressed kernel 12% larger (6.4 instead of
5.7 MB), well within what the boot loader loads:

  fork               690 -> 510 us
  fork + exec       1946 -> 1534 us
  loopback TCP       306 -> 365 MB/s
  pipe round trip   17.0 -> 15.5 us
  system call        289 -> 278 ns

Build it for performance, the default.
---
 arch/mips/configs/ad5x_defconfig | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/configs/ad5x_defconfig b/arch/mips/configs/ad5x_defconfig
index 495621263..234ade8ca 100644
--- a/arch/mips/configs/ad5x_defconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/configs/ad5x_defconfig
@@ -4,7 +4,6 @@ CONFIG_HIGH_RES_TIMERS=y
 CONFIG_PREEMPT=y
 CONFIG_IKCONFIG=y
 CONFIG_IKCONFIG_PROC=y
-CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE=y
 CONFIG_EXPERT=y
 CONFIG_KALLSYMS_ALL=y
 CONFIG_MACH_INGENIC_SOC=y
